## Where to hang “scope warning” logic

| Surface | `teacher_id` | `subject` | Grade / student context |
|--------|--------------|-----------|-------------------------|
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/components/CourseEditForm.vue` | `form.teacher_id` (native `<select>`) | `form.subject` | None — use parent’s `selectedStudent.grade` (e.g. in `StudentsList` when editing). |
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/components/UniversalClassScheduler.vue` | `form.teacher_id` (`SearchableSelect`) | `form.subject` | `form.student_id` — resolve grade from `props.students` (or API). |
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/StudentsList.vue` | Passed into `CourseEditForm` as `teachers`; edit flow uses `submitCourse` body `teacher_id` | `courseForm.subject` | Student grade: `studentForm.grade` (student modal) or `selectedStudent.value?.grade` for the course being edited. |
| `/home/admin/frontend/src/components/EnrollmentWizard.vue` | `courseForm.teacher_id` | `courseForm.subject` | `studentForm.grade` (new student) or existing student record when chosen. |

**Note:** With the current template, **new course** creation from the list uses **`UniversalClassScheduler`**, not `CourseEditForm`; the `submitCourse` branch for `!editingCourseId` is only relevant if some code path still opens that flow without the scheduler (otherwise it is effectively unused for the visible “新增” UI).

